  "id": "586bbfc0-b191-46c8-a532-82ea2185f7ee",
  "title": "FSSAI Revises Food Labelling Norms for Nutrients",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court of India has asked the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) to revise front-of-pack labelling norms for nutrients of concern, including total sugars and saturated fats, rather than added sugar and fat. The court also directs the FSSAI to introduce separate warning labels for these nutrients to enhance consumer awareness and food safety.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court of India has asked FSSAI to treat ‘total sugars’ and ‘saturated fat’ as the nutrients of concern",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court directs the FSSAI to recalculate thresholds for nutrients of concern",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The FSSAI is expected to introduce separate warning labels for these nutrients in packaged foods",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
